1. The generated DEXPI classes (pydexpi/pydexpi_classes/)
---------------------------------------------------------

The Pydantic classes in pydexpi/pydexpi_classes/ -- pydexpi_classes.py, _spec_info.py and the
core/, plant/ and process/ modules; not the hand-written _base.py and unit_resolution.py -- are
generated from the DEXPI Specification 2.0.1, (c) 2026 DEXPI (DEXPI e.V.), licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.

Source: https://gitlab.com/dexpi/Specification/-/releases/V2.0.1 (tag V2.0.1, commit
eef0f0c6e8edfe84582e7a45d109c396bdc544f8): its machine-readable model, Dexpi.xmi, and the model
files the specification's own build writes (Core.xml, Plant.xml, Process.xml, Builtin.xml), as
vendored with their provenance in pyDEXPI-builder
(https://github.com/process-intelligence-research/pyDEXPI-builder, data/dexpi_xmi_files/2.0.1/).

The classes are an adaptation of the specification. Changes:

- the model is translated to Pydantic, with Python names (TagName becomes tagName, and a name
  the generated classes reserve gets a trailing underscore: Role.Uri becomes uri_, which keeps
  Uri as its dexpi_name);
- the data types that parent enumerations (PhysicalQuantityUnit, PressureUnit, FrequencyUnit)
  are generated as enumerations;
- the documentation is the specification's reStructuredText text, with the specificator's own
  roles (:sp:element: and :sp:name:) rendered as the text they name and standard roles kept
  verbatim; each description is joined onto one line, and LaTeX-style \url{...} becomes a plain
  URL;
- the multiplicities of the opposite ends of associations are not generated;
- three semantic deviations from the specification, each declared with its reason and evidence
  in pyDEXPI-builder's SPEC_DEVIATIONS table, and marked on the field it changes as
  "spec_deviation" in its json_schema_extra:
  - QV-VALUE-UNION: QualifiedValue.Value is
    float | int | PhysicalQuantity | PhysicalQuantityVector | Undefined (required), the union of
    the types the specification's bindings give it, instead of the declared
    PhysicalQuantity | Double;
  - PORT-SUBREFERENCE: Port.SubReference is a reference, not a composition;
  - COMPONENT-ORDER: ListOfMaterialComponents.Component is an ordered list.

The header of pydexpi_classes.py and the docstring of pydexpi/pydexpi_classes/__init__.py carry
the same attribution.


2. The DEXPI reference P&ID (data/reference_pid.xml, data/reference_pid.json)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

data/reference_pid.xml contains material of the DEXPI Specification 2.0 -- its reference P&ID --
(c) 2025 DEXPI (DEXPI e.V.), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
License (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.

Source: https://gitlab.com/dexpi/Specification/-/releases/V2.0.0.

Changes: the one content change is that eight Shape objects that carry no
SymbolRegistrationNumber in the original were given the placeholder value
MISSING_IN_ORIGINAL_EXAMPLE_FILE (pyDEXPI commit 1325ac13). Otherwise the file is XML-equivalent
to the original: five empty strings are written <String/> rather than <String></String>, and the
file has no final newline (pyDEXPI commit e1413dc9).
data/reference_pid.json is the same document converted to pyDEXPI's JSON format by pyDEXPI.


