7. The process tables (pydexpi/toolkits/process_toolkit.py)
-----------------------------------------------------------

PORT_CONNECTIONS, PORT_ROLE_NAMES and ABSTRACT_PROCESS_CLASSES in
pydexpi/toolkits/process_toolkit.py transcribe material of the DEXPI Specification 2.0.1, (c) 2026
DEXPI (DEXPI e.V.), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/: which port class each process
connection class joins, the role names each port class lists, and which process classes are
abstract.

Source: https://gitlab.com/dexpi/Specification/-/releases/V2.0.1 (tag V2.0.1, commit
eef0f0c6e8edfe84582e7a45d109c396bdc544f8), the class descriptions and declarations in
src/model/Process/Process/Process.py, cited by line in the module.

Changes: transcribed into Python tables; nothing added to them. DEFAULT_ROLES beside them is
pyDEXPI's own choice among the listed names, not specification material.


